<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Peters Humphrey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1905">1905</a>–<a href="/years/1995">1995</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Peters Humphrey was a Canadian legal scholar at McGill University who served as the first director of the Human Rights Division of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> Secretariat from 1946 to 1966. He prepared the first draft of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/universal-declaration-of-human-rights">Universal Declaration of Human Rights</a>, adopted in 1948, and later helped found Amnesty International <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> and other human rights bodies.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…build post-war institutions: Lester B. Pearson won the Nobel Peace Prize in 1957 for proposing the United Nations Emergency Force during the Suez Crisis, which set the pattern for armed peacekeeping, and the lawyer <b>John Peters Humphrey</b> prepared the first draft of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights.</blockquote><a href="/empire/canada">Canada · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Hampton, in what is now <a href="/countries/canada">Canada</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/canada">Canada</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=45.53,-65.83&amp;year=1963" aria-label="Hampton on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2989 558 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of John Peters Humphrey"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3439 828h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3439 828h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=45.53,-65.83&amp;year=1963">What was here in 1963? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
